"Bluetooth and USB are off until you turn them on. Neither needs a permission Flowlight doesn't already have — they're off because watching them widens what the app looks at, and that should be your decision rather than something an update did.\n\nNeither can report bytes. macOS keeps no per-app accounting for these channels, so what Flowlight can honestly show is what is connected, which apps are built to use it, and when that changed." = "藍牙和 USB 要等你開啟才會作用。兩者都不需要 Flowlight 還沒有的權限 — 預設關閉是因為監看它們會擴大這個 App 觀察的範圍，而這應該由你決定，不該是某次更新替你決定的。\n\n兩者都無法回報位元組數。macOS 不會為這些通道記錄各 App 的用量，所以 Flowlight 能誠實顯示的，是有什麼連著、哪些 App 本來就會用它，以及這些狀況何時改變。";
"No byte counts on these channels. macOS keeps no per-app accounting for Bluetooth or USB, so a figure here would be invented. What is honest is what's connected, which apps are built to use it, and when that changed." = "這些通道沒有位元組計數。macOS 不會為藍牙或 USB 記錄各 App 的用量，所以這裡若出現數字也只是編出來的。能誠實呈現的，是有什麼連著、哪些 App 本來就會用它，以及這些狀況何時改變。";
"This is each app saying so in its own Info.plist — who asked for Bluetooth, not who macOS granted it to. That second list lives in a database an app can't read, and Flowlight would rather name the difference than blur it." = "這是各 App 在自己的 Info.plist 中宣告的 — 是誰要求使用藍牙，而不是 macOS 把權限給了誰。後者記在一個 App 讀不到的資料庫裡，而 Flowlight 寧可把這個差別說清楚，也不願含糊帶過。";
"How Flowlight recognises this device between sightings" = "Flowlight 如何在不同次出現之間認出這個裝置";

